''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]'' returned for its twenty-first series with a launch show on 16 September 2023 on [[BBC One]], with live shows beginning on 23 September.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://uk.sports.yahoo.com/news/strictly-come-dancing-everything-fans-060009536.html|title=Strictly Come Dancing: Everything Fans Need To Know About This Year's Series|publisher=[[Yahoo!]]|date=26 August 2023|accessdate=26 August 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Launch Show |url=https://bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly-launch-show-6sept23 |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |archive-date=21 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230721122758/https://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/strictly-launch-show-6sept23 |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Tess Daly]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned as hosts, while [[Janette Manrara]] returned to host ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]'', alongside [[Fleur East]], who was announced as the new co-host after [[Rylan Clark]]'s departure in April 2023.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Glynn |first1=Paul |title=Rylan Clark steps down from Strictly Come Dancing spin-off It Takes Two |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-65248559 |work=[[BBC News]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=12 April 2023 |archive-date=14 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230514071118/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-65248559 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Moss |first1=Molly |title=Strictly It Takes Two confirms Fleur East as new host and Rylan responds to replacement |url=https://radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-it-takes-two-host-fleur-east-rylan-replacement-newsupdate/ |work=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=17 June 2023 |archive-date=28 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230628225833/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-it-takes-two-host-fleur-east-rylan-replacement-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In April 2023, the BBC announced that [[Shirley Ballas]], [[Anton Du Beke]], [[Motsi Mabuse]], and [[Craig Revel Horwood]] would return to the judging panel.<ref name="Judges and professionals">{{cite news |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2023 Professional Dancers, Judges, Presenters and more confirmed |url=https://bbc.com/mediacentre/2023/strictly-come-dancing-2023-professional-dancers-judges-presenters-confirmed |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=21 April 2023 |archive-date=21 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230721122811/https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2023/strictly-come-dancing-2023-professional-dancers-judges-presenters-confirmed |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Earp |first1=Catherine |title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms 2023 judges and professional dancer line-up |url=https://digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a43664733/strictly-2023-judges-professional-dancer-line-up/ |work=[[Digital Spy]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=21 April 2023 |archive-date=8 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230608112357/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a43664733/strictly-2023-judges-professional-dancer-line-up/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Actress [[Ellie Leach]] and her partner [[Vito Coppola]] were announced as the winners on 16 December,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-67726020 |title=Strictly Come Dancing 2023: Winner of glitterball trophy announced|date=16 December 2023|work=BBC News|accessdate=18 December 2023}}</ref> while [[Layton Williams]] and [[Nikita Kuzmin]], and [[Bobby Brazier]] and [[Dianne Buswell]] were the runners-up.

