The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. The couples are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the lowest scored couple receiving one point, and the highest scored couple receiving the most points (the maximum number of points available depends on the number of couples remaining in the competition). The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; the couple with the fewest votes receiving one point, and the couple with the most votes receiving the most points.

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave, with [[Shirley Ballas]], as head judge, having the last and [[Casting vote|deciding vote]] if needed.

== Professional dancers ==
In April 2023, the BBC announced that [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Nadiya Bychkova]], [[Vito Coppola]], [[Graziano Di Prima]], [[Amy Dowden]], [[Carlos Gu]], [[Karen Hauer]], [[Katya Jones]], [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Nikita Kuzmin]], [[Gorka Márquez]], [[Luba Mushtuk]], [[Lauren Oakley]], [[Giovanni Pernice]], [[Jowita Przystał]], [[Johannes Radebe]], [[Michelle Tsiakkas]], [[Kai Widdrington]], and [[Nancy Xu]] would be returning to the series.<ref name="Judges and professionals" /><ref>{{cite news |title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms 2023 professionals as one exits show |url=https://radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-confirms-2023-professionals-newsupdate/ |last=Cremona |first=Patrick |work=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=21 April 2023 |archive-date=4 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604001654/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-confirms-2023-professionals-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The only professional dancer who did not return was [[Cameron Lombard]], who had been part of the professional group routines since the [[Strictly Come Dancing (series 19)|nineteenth series]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Strictly Come Dancing professional Cameron Lombard confirms he's quit the show |url=https://digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a43666539/strictly-professional-cameron-lombard-quits/ |last=Rowan |first=Iona |work=[[Digital Spy]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=21 April 2023 |archive-date=8 June 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230608112343/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a43666539/strictly-professional-cameron-lombard-quits/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Welsh |first1=Daniel |title=Strictly Bids Farewell To Cameron Lombard As This Year's Professional Line-Up Is Confirmed |url=https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/strictly-come-dancing-loses-professional-dancer-2023-line-up_uk_64427f02e4b0408f3e52b664 |work=[[HuffPost]] |access-date=20 July 2023 |date=21 April 2023 |archive-date=5 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230505135542/https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/amp/entry/strictly-come-dancing-loses-professional-dancer-2023-line-up_uk_64427f02e4b0408f3e52b664/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In May 2023, Dowden announced she had been diagnosed with [[Grading (tumors)|grade III]] [[breast cancer]] and underwent a [[mastectomy]], but added she was "determined" to get back on the dance floor and that she was hoping to take part in the series if she was able to.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly's Amy Dowden reveals breast cancer diagnosis |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-wales-65682699 |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=21 July 2023 |date=24 May 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/may/24/amy-dowden-breast-cancer-diagnosis-strictly-come-dancing|title=Strictly star Amy Dowden announces breast cancer diagnosis|work=The Guardian|date=24 May 2023|accessdate=24 May 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Amy Dowden shares update on Strictly Come Dancing future after breast cancer diagnosis |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/amy-dowden-strictly-cancer-update-2023-b2360139.html |website=[[The Independent]]|date=19 June 2023 }}</ref> Despite her initial plans to return for the series, Dowden confirmed in July that she had been diagnosed with "another type of cancer" and would be unable to partner a celebrity due to undergoing [[chemotherapy]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing pro Amy Dowden shares devastating update as doctors find 'more tumours' amid breast cancer treatment |url=https://metro.co.uk/2023/07/21/strictly-pro-amy-dowden-needs-chemo-as-doctors-find-more-tumours-after-scan-19172152/ |website=[[Metro (British newspaper)|Metro]] |access-date=21 July 2023 |date=21 July 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Wright |first1=Minnie |title=Amy Dowden won't be in main Strictly line-up amid further cancer diagnosis |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/amy-dowden-strictly-come-dancing-2023-second-cancer-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=22 July 2023 |date=22 July 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly's Amy reveals her second cancer diagnosis |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cd1e7j8kqllo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=22 July 2023 |date=22 July 2023}}</ref>

During the launch show, Lauren Oakley received a celebrity partner for the first time, while Neil Jones, Nadiya Bychkova, and Michelle Tsiakkas did not receive a partner. The rest of the pros were paired to a celebrity, including Luba Mushtuk, who did not have a celebrity partner for the last two series.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/tv/bbc-strictly-come-dancing-2023-27726792|title=BBC Strictly Come Dancing 2023: Full list of celebrities and professional partners|work=[[Manchester Evening News]]|first1=Jessica|last1=Sansome|first2=Phoebe|last2=Jobling|date=16 September 2023|accessdate=17 September 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hellomagazine.com/film/502589/strictly-come-dancing-lauren-oakley-everything-you-need-to-know/|title=Who is Strictly's Lauren Oakley? All of the details about pro|work=[[Hello! (magazine)|Hello!]]|first=Megan|last=Bull|date=16 September 2023|accessdate=17 September 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref>

==Couples==
This series features fifteen celebrity contestants. On 4 August 2023, the first three celebrities announced as participants in the series were [[Amanda Abbington]], [[Angela Rippon]], and [[Layton Williams]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/aug/04/angela-rippon-to-be-oldest-strictly-come-dancing-contestant|title=Angela Rippon to be oldest Strictly Come Dancing contestant|website=[[The Guardian]]|first=Nadeem|last=Badshah|date=4 August 2023|access-date=4 August 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref> Celebrity contestants continued to be revealed until 11 August 2023, when the full line-up was announced.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-66408141|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2023: Entertainer Les Dennis completes line-up|publisher=[[BBC]]|first=Helen|last=Bushby|date=11 August 2023|access-date=11 August 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/strictly-come-dancing-2023-line-up-contestants/|title=Strictly Come Dancing 2023 line-up: Full cast of contestants confirmed|website=[[Radio Times]]|first1=Grace|last1=Henry|first2=Sophie|last2=Cockerham|first3=Lewis|last3=Knight|date=11 August 2023|access-date=11 August 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref>

On 23 October, it was announced that [[Amanda Abbington]] had withdrawn from the competition after having missed the previous week.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2023/oct/23/amanda-abbington-quits-strictly-come-dancing-medical-absence|title=Amanda Abbington quits Strictly Come Dancing after medical absence|website=[[The Guardian]]|first=Nadeem|last=Badshah|date=23 October 2023|access-date=23 October 2023|language=en-GB}}</ref>

On 2 December, hours before the live episode was set to air, it was announced that [[Nigel Harman]] had been forced to withdraw from the competition due to a rib injury.<ref name=":2" />
